---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Terms — ChordPlane"
  description="The terms that cover using the ChordPlane app, the shared-link service and this website."
>
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p>Plain terms for a small app. Using ChordPlane means you accept them.</p>
    <p class="updated">Last updated 21 November 2026</p>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose">
    <h2>The app</h2>
    <p>
      ChordPlane is a chord and lyric songbook for Android. It is provided free
      of charge, as is, without warranty of any kind. It may change, and it may
      contain bugs.
    </p>

    <h2>Your content</h2>
    <p>
      Songs, arrangements and set lists you create or import remain yours. You
      are responsible for them, including making sure you have the right to
      store and share the lyrics and arrangements involved.
    </p>

    <h2>Share links</h2>
    <p>
      Share links are readable by anyone who has the URL. Only share material
      you are allowed to distribute. Links may be removed if they are used for
      unlawful or infringing content, or to abuse the service.
    </p>

    <h2>Accounts</h2>
    <p>
      Keep your sign-in details to yourself. You are responsible for activity
      under your account. You can stop using the service at any time and ask for
      your account to be deleted.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Don't use the service to break the law or infringe someone's rights.</li>
      <li>Don't attempt to disrupt it, probe it for vulnerabilities without permission, or use it to store unrelated files.</li>
      <li>Don't automate sign-ups or share-creation at a volume that degrades the service for others.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Availability</h2>
    <p>
      The shared-link service is best-effort. There is no uptime guarantee, and
      links are not a backup — keep your own copies of anything you would miss.
    </p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by law, ChordPlane is not liable for lost data,
      missed performances, or any indirect loss arising from use of the app or
      the service.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may be updated as the app changes. The date at the top of the
      page reflects the current version.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Anything unclear?
      <a href="https://github.com/danny192168/ChordPlane-v2/issues" rel="noopener"
        >Open an issue on GitHub</a
      >.
    </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
